finding: Stage 1, HEAD 0d3417f8: findings (no worktree files edited). P2 — crates/audio/src/sample.rs:14-15 — claim 1, newly stated out-of-range contract is false. “Returns silence outside the buffer” has no finite/range precondition. sample_read(&[1.0], f64::MAX) panics, not silence: the float-to-usize cast saturates, then i + 1 overflows at line 22 in debug; in release it wraps and buffer[i - 1] panics at line 26. Independently reproduced against this exact source with rustc in both debug and -O (also reproduced with +infinity). The repro used a dummy hermite4, which is never reached. This is a false newly added contract, not a request to change numerical behavior; qualify the supported positions/panic behavior or describe the implemented boundary behavior accurately. P2 — crates/physics/src/arena.rs:288-289 — the claimed colorSpan stale-claim correction is incomplete. Remaining documentation says “The active colors' spans, as written by TS `writeColorSpans`”. No such TS writer exists in the tree (repository search); solve.rs:529-530 gets its spans from constraint_graph::solver_colors into local span_storage instead. Removing the same claim at solve_build did not sweep this declaration. This is an existing false ownership/producer claim left in the stage's scope, not a newly introduced regression. P3 — crates/native/src/helper.rs:1-4; crates/physics/scripts/build-kernel.ts:7-18 — claim 4, walkthrough/history/emphasis remains outside tests/oracles/fixtures. helper.rs still opens with “running this binary: load the framework (helper layout), then hand off to execute_process, which runs the subprocess loop and returns when it exits.” The operations are immediately visible below; retain only the otherwise non-obvious subprocess/platform requirement, not their walkthrough. build-kernel.ts still gives an extended two-artifact narrative including “Every host gets this; it is the shipping path and must never move” and “this is a toolchain switch, not a code change.” These are unswept production build-script comments within crates/, not port source symbols or undecidable blocks listed for escalation. The scope is not just changed Rust files. Independent examination: - Read the unit, CONTRIBUTING.md (including 270-273), nine stage commits, and rendering reference 04f07830..ecfbc0b3/556e0975's restoration scope. - Read the entire crates diff block by block; identified and examined the 25 largest hunks plus 25 others selected deterministically with Python Random(1) from the remainder. Additional current-code examination concentrated on col's constructor/Send/Sync/atomic contracts, stages' CAS/barrier/orchestration/fault paths, solve's build/finalize/parallel-for joins, ParFor sizing and claim loop, graph removal order and color producer, and audio read edges. - Claim 2: no independently established loss of an actionable non-obvious fact in that sample. In particular col retains constructor-wide obligations, lifetime and stationary-storage requirements; stages retains aliasing, disjointness, claim reuse, barriers and handle-lifetime requirements. Not a proof of all unchanged comments or every algorithmic fact. - Verified the stored-order correction against graph swap_remove and serial overflow range traversal; creation order was not preserved. Verified ParFor::run's one-return-is-not-a-barrier correction against its fetch_add claim loop and scheduler finish calls. Verified finalize is outside stages::walk and reached through Job::Finalize after run_solve's solver/split joins. The colorSpan correction is locally valid in solve.rs but incomplete as reported above. - Claim 3 clean: all added/deleted nonblank lines outside allowed regenerated artifacts classify as comments (including TOML); diff --check passes. Independently rebuilt both physics artifacts and audio from a git archive of HEAD in /tmp, leaving this worktree unchanged. cmp is byte-identical for kernel.wasm.ts, kernel.shared.wasm.ts, shallot_audio.js, shallot_audio.wasm and shal